  "methodology_note": "The raw residual effect size (mean/std of actual-reference, P10's bias statistic) is NOT the detector for this mechanism: an exponent truncation multiplies each output element by 1/(m_a*m_b), and a multiplicative shrink of a near-zero-mean output leaves a near-zero-mean residual. Both statistics are reported; the decision uses the per-row projection slope <actual,ref>/<ref,ref>, which is n-invariant and is exactly what a gain error moves. frob-rel (magnitude-weighted L2), never an elementwise max, is used for size -- a below-RMS e4m3 output element can show a large relative delta from rounding alone.",
